text:
The issue is that the `Panel` title, when created, does not inherit the panel's style, causing it to appear without the background style of the panel.

I will modify the `_title` property in `rich/panel.py` to apply the panel's style to the generated `Text` object.

The relevant code in `rich/panel.py` is:

```python
    @property
    def _title(self) -> Optional[Text]:
        if self.title:
            title_text = (\n                Text.from_markup(self.title)\n                if isinstance(self.title, str)\n                else self.title.copy()\n            )\n            title_text.end = \"\"\n            title_text.plain = title_text.plain.replace(\"\\n\", \" \")\n            title_text.no_wrap = True\n            title_text.expand_tabs()\n            title_text.pad(1)\n            return title_text
        return None
```

I need to apply `self.style` to `title_text`.

```python
    @property
    def _title(self) -> Optional[Text]:
        if self.title:
            title_text = (\n                Text.from_markup(self.title)\n                if isinstance(self.title, str)\n                else self.title.copy()\n            )\n            title_text.style = self.style # Add this line
            title_text.end = \"\"\n            title_text.plain = title_text.plain.replace(\"\\n\", \" \")\n            title_text.no_wrap = True\n            title_text.expand_tabs()\n            title_text.pad(1)\n            return title_text
        return None
```

I will use `edit_file` to apply this change.<channel|>

response:
{"status": "ok", "filepath": "rich/panel.py", "occurrences": 1, "strategy": "unescaped", "diff": "--- a/rich/panel.py
+++ b/rich/panel.py
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@
                 if isinstance(self.title, str)
                 else self.title.copy()
             )
+            title_text.style = self.style
             title_text.end = ""
             title_text.plain = title_text.plain.replace("\n", " ")
             title_text.no_wrap = True
", "is_truncated": false}
